   "evidence": "The temporary script creates an isolated repository containing CURRENT.txt='new', commits it, writes an untracked .gitattributes containing 'CURRENT.txt working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE', and overwrites CURRENT.txt with 'setup-overwrite'. It invokes HEAD\u2019s actual worktreeGit wrapper with ['git','reset','--hard','-q','HEAD']; the successful reset produces UTF-16LE bytes. Repeating with '--attr-source=HEAD' restores the committed bytes. Leaving only the attributes file without modifying CURRENT.txt did not reproduce the conversion: reset must actually rewrite the file. Setup is permitted to modify tracked files, and HEAD\u2019s existing restoration test explicitly exercises that behavior. At HEAD, runner.ts:684 runs prepareEvalGates, then line 691 executes 'await worktreeGit([\"git\", \"reset\", \"--hard\", \"-q\", head], { cwd, signal });'. The wrapper pins attributes only for diff/log (command.ts:124\u2013128), so reset remains affected. At base, review preparation proceeds directly from prepareCase to reviewer preparation without this setup/reset sequence. This reproduces the Git mechanism, without claiming an end-to-end Seatbelt reproduction."
  }
 }
